# The pipeline's approval ledger (_management/approvals.json) sha-pins Markdown
# deliverables (dramaturgy, motion scripts, visual prompts, concept notes) to their
# LF-on-disk bytes, and the validator suite (tests/pipeline_integrity.py
# sha256_file) reads the working-tree bytes. On Windows with core.autocrlf=true a
# checkout/merge can materialize a .md file with CRLF, drifting it off its recorded
# LF sha and firing a false gate FAIL (or tempting a re-pin to a CRLF sha that then
# breaks Linux CI). Force LF for the sha-pinned text types so every platform sees
# the same bytes the ledger recorded.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
